.TH UU-REMOTE-VIRTUAL-DISPLAYCTL 1 "@RELEASE_DATE@" "uu-remote-for-linux @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uu-remote-virtual-displayctl \- manage the UU Remote X11 virtual display
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uu-remote-virtual-displayctl
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Controls the per-user
.B uu-remote-virtual-displayd
service over an authenticated Unix socket.
The service serializes NVIDIA XRandR operations, preserves the requested mode,
and restores the virtual output after display-stack drift or a service restart.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print the desired state, live backend state, stable display identifier, and diagnostics as JSON.
.TP
.B create
Enable the virtual display.  Accepts
.BR --mode ,
.BR --rate ,
and
.BR --rotation .
.TP
.B update
Change one or more properties of an active virtual display.
.TP
.B remove
Disable the virtual display and persist the off state.
.TP
.B recover
Reconcile the live XRandR state with the persisted desired state immediately.
.TP
.B ping
Check service availability and print its current status.
.TP
.B wait
Wait up to 60 seconds for the requested
.BR active ,
.BR off ,
or
.B fault
state.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/uu-remote-for-linux/virtual-display.sock
Per-user control socket, mode 0600.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/uu-remote-for-linux/virtual-displayd-status.json
Current daemon and backend status.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/uu-remote-for-linux/virtual-displayd-desired.json
Persisted desired display state.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/uu-remote-for-linux/virtual-displayd.log
Service log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xrandr (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR uu-remote-for-linux (1)
